How it works

<p>
    All content is rated on a <b>0–10 scale</b>, allowing more nuance than simple upvotes.
</p>

<ul>
    <li><b>0</b> = not useful or not important</li>
    <li><b>10</b> = highly valuable or worth attention</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Each item shows:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Average score</li>
    <li>Your score</li>
    <li>Total votes</li>
</ul>

<p>
    This helps prioritize ideas based on <b>quality, impact, and relevance</b>.
</p>


<p>
    This platform is built around <b>issues and solutions</b>.
</p>

<p>
    They can be:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Global (climate change, public policy)</li>
    <li>Local (community needs, infrastructure)</li>
    <li>Personal (health, education, daily life)</li>
    <li>Creative (projects, ideas, experiments)</li>
</ul>

<p>
    If it matters to someone, it belongs here.
</p>